{"Buj": [{"id": "Buj", "headword": "भुज्", "headword_slp1": "Buj", "fold": "Buj", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "1. भुज् cl. 6. P. (Dhātup. xxviii, 124) भुज॑ति (pf. बुभोज aor. अभौक्षीत् fut. भोक्ष्यति and ˚क्ता Gr.; really only pr. stem aor. -अ॑बुभोजीस् and ind.p. -भुज्य after निर् and परि; cf. also भुजम् in भुजं-ग and भुजंगम),\nto bend, curve;\n (?) to sweep (cf. 1. भुजि॑), RV. :\nPass. भुज्यते, to be bent down or disheartened, Hit. iv, 28.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "भुज् [cf. Gk. ϕεύγω; Lat. fugio; Goth. biugan, baugjan (?); Germ. biogan, biegen; Angl.Sax. búgan; Eng. bow.]", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "2. भुज् See त्रि-भु॑ज्.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "3. भुज् cl. 7. P. Ā. (Dhātup. xxix, 17) भुन॑क्ति, भुङ्क्ते॑\n(rarely cl. 6. P. Ā. भुञ्जति, ˚ते, Up.; MBh.;\n3. pl. Ā. भुञ्जते॑, RV.;\nPot. P. भुञ्जीयात्, Gobh.;\npf. Ā. बुभुजे॑, ˚ज्म॑हे, ˚ज्रिरे॑, RV.;\n3. pl. P. ˚जुः, MBh.;\naor. अभौक्षीत्, अभुक्त Gr.;\nभो॑जम्, भो॑जते, भुजेम, RV.;\nभुक्षिषीय, Br.;\nfut. भोक्ष्यति, ˚ते, MBh. &c.;\nभोक्ता, R.;\ninf. भो॑जसे, भु॑जम्, भुजे, RV. : भोक्तुम्, MBh. &c.;\nind.p. भुक्त्वा or भुङ्क्त्वा, ib.),\nto enjoy, use, possess, (esp.) enjoy a meal, eat, eat and drink, consume (mostly Ā.; in Ved. generally with instr., later with acc.), RV. &c. &c. ;\nto enjoy (carnally), Gṛhyās.; MBh.; Kāv.;\nto make use of, utilize, exploit, Mn.; MBh. &c.;\n (with पृथिवीम्, महीम् &c.) to take possession of, rule, govern, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;\nto suffer, experience, undergo, be requited or rewarded for (acc.) or at the hands of (gen.), RV. &c. &c.;\n (P.) to be of use or service to (acc.), RV.; TS.; Br.; Up.;\nto pass, live through, last (a time), Rājat.; BhP.;\n (in astron.) to pass through, fulfil, Sūryas. :\nPass. भुज्यते (aor. अभोजि), to be enjoyed or eaten or possessed or made use of Br.; MBh. &c.:\nCaus. भोजयति (ते˚, mc.; cf. Pāṇ. i, 3, 87; once भुञ्जापयति, Pañcat. ii, 49 v.l.; aor. अबूभुजत्, ˚जत Gr.),\nto cause to enjoy or eat, feed with (two acc. or acc. of pers. and instr. of thing; cf. Pāṇ. i, 4, 52), AV. &c.;\n &c.;\nto use as food, Car. :\nDesid. बुभुक्षति (once), ˚ते, to wish to eat, be hungry, MBh.; BhP.;\nto wish to enjoy or partake of Naiṣ. (cf. बुभुक्षा, ˚क्षित, ˚क्षु) :\nIntens. बोभुज्यते, to be eaten frequently, VarBṛS.;\n बोभोक्ति and बोभुजीति, to eat or enjoy frequently Gr.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "भुज् [cf. Lat. fungor.]", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "4. भु॑ज् f. enjoyment, profit, advantage, possession or use of (gen.), RV.; AV. (भुजे॑, also as infin.)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "भु॑ज् m. an enjoyer, eater (said of Agni), RV. x, 20, 2", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "भु॑ज् mfn. (ifc.) enjoying (also carnally), eating, consuming, partaking of, possessing, ruling, Mn.; MBh. and o. (with words meaning ‘earth’ = ‘king’; cf. क्षितिभ्˚ &c.)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "भु॑ज् m. enjoying the reward of, suffering for (किल्बिष-भ्˚), MārkP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "passing, through, fulfilling (व्यक्त-भ्˚), BhP.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "Buja": [{"id": "Buja", "headword": "भुज", "headword_slp1": "Buja", "fold": "Buja", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "भुज m. (ifc. f(आ). ) the arm, MBh.; Kāv. &c. (भुजयोर् अन्तरम्, the breast, Bhartṛ.; cf. भुजान्तर)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the hand, Pāṇ. vii, 3, 61", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the trunk of an elephant, MBh. iii, 15736", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a branch, bough, BhP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a bending, curve, coil (of a serpent; see comp. below)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the side of any geometrical figure, KātyŚr., Sch.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the base of a triangle, Sūryas.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the base of a shadow, ib.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the supplement of 2 or 4 right angles or the complement of 3 right angles, MW.", "gloss_lang